%I A397142 #17 Jul 29 2026 21:26:57
%S A397142 1,2,3,11,22,111,121,212,1111,11111,11211,111111,1111111,11111111,
%T A397142 111111111
%N A397142 Palindromes without digit 0 whose square is also a palindrome.
%C A397142 Theorem: The square of a palindrome P is also a palindrome iff the sum of the squares of the digits of P is less than 10 (see Diophante link).
%C A397142 From this sequence, we obtain the palindromes with digit 0 such that the square is also a palindrome, by adding 0's to each term to obtain new palindromes. For example, from 212, we obtain 20102, 2001002, 200010002, ... .
%H A397142 Diophante, <a href="http://www.diophante.fr/problemes-par-themes/arithmetique-et-algebre/a3-nombres-remarquables/3333-2015-11-04-21-45-38">A317 = Palindromes et leurs carrés palindromes</a> (in French).
%e A397142 111111111^2 = 12345678987654321, so 111111111 is a term.
%Y A397142 Intersection of A057135 and A052382.
%Y A397142 Cf. A104075 (subsequence of repdigits).
%K A397142 nonn,fini,full
%O A397142 1,2
%A A397142 _Bernard Schott_, Jul 21 2026
